Z||000011||Monkeyman||12-29-1999||11:59 PM||||I can't believe that elementary schools have computers now.  (I mean for the students to use.)  I was a junior in high school before I even saw one in school.  Damn, I feel old!  No wonder I need medication! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Cooter--Have you ever heard of "Trucker Buddys"?  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||12-30-1999||12:06 AM||||The county system gave us a Pentium 2-333 and networked every school in our system for e-mail and internet. Let me tell you, internet over a T-1 line kicks butt! The other computers in the room are mine, 7 in all for my kids to use. I have more at home, but no place in my classroom to put them! <BR>Trucker Buddies is like pen pals isnt it?||||reg||1
Z||000013||2FAST4U||12-30-1999||01:27 AM||||Computers in school?<BR>WOW<BR>When I finished High School in Decatur Ala calculating any number larger than 10 required taking off your shoes and using your toes. They were talking about calculators in Popular Science magazine, They were about the size of a school bus. And before you say anything Monkeyman, Yes we had shoes in Alabama then, but we only wore them to school and church.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Call||12-30-1999||02:06 AM||||Im runnin a ADSL Connection into my house, and let me tell you, it is NICE. I get around 1 megabyte a second, I enjoy every minute of it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||10
