Z||000022||fiero56||01-01-2000||09:20 PM||||Here is my very uninspiring site: <A HREF="http://www.geocities/motorcity/pit/3490/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities/motorcity/pit/3490/index.html</A> <BR>I will be adding to this as time permits.<P>Starting back when I was in middle school(6th grade) there were these "technology" levies for our school system. Anything the school system asked to have the community vote on, parents and voters accepted it. Well, it wasn't too long before the schools had more money than they knew what to do with. We had 2 tv's in each classroom, and computers were being added daily. By the time I graduated (june '99) we had t1 lines running all over the place, tv's everywhere, and all classes had at least 2 computers, depending on classroom size, some teachers got a dozen or more. All computers were pentium II's, all souped up. A networking nightmare. <BR>Now I'm stuck with my laptop/notebook computer. 56K and 200mmx mhz isn't very excillerating anymore.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||Cooter||01-01-2000||11:06 PM||||I am the tech. coordinator for my school and we have gone all year without a computer lab. Long story, mainly a classroom was needed last year so the lab was used and the computers were divided up amoung the teachers that wanted one (p75's). Now, we have been given a couple of grants and some federal money- I have a working budget of about $42,000 to set up a new lab for next year. Unfortunatly, everything must be purchased off the state/county bid list. If I could order from other venders, I could get twice as much stuff, or save half the money for updates/software. I am open to suggestions on what kind of equipment to buy.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Monkeyman||01-02-2000||02:01 AM||||Ummm...You could get an awful lot of Commodore 64s with that kind of money.<P>.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000025||batboy||01-02-2000||08:00 AM||||For a school computer lab, it would be hard to beat the Celeron CPU chip prices when buying new computers.<P>Back to the website subject, there's no reason we couldn't sort of make our own little Fiero Forum webring. We just need to make a page on each site that links to all the other Fiero Forum member's webpages.||||reg||1
